  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "作業系統(一)",
    "sub_ename": "OPERATING SYSTEMS(1)",
    "describe_ch": "本課程旨在介紹電腦作業系統的內部組成與運作原理，也就是電腦系統內部管理的相關知識。課程內容包括作業系統的基本介紹與回顧，與硬體相關的介面需求，然後對於作業系統的各項組成元件模組，如行程管理，CPU排班，行程同步與死結，主記憶體的管理，虛擬記憶體機制的結構與運作，分別詳細解說。\n 本課程要求學生結合課程所學，前往校外社區、中小學、公益機構等單位，進行12小時的「服務學習」。",
    "describe_eh": "This course is aimed to introduce the principles of internal structure and operations of operating systems. The contents include the background and overview of operating systems, the requirements of hardware support and interface to operating systems, and the detailed discussion into each operating system component, like Process Management, CPU Scheduling, Process Coordination and Deadlock, Main Memory Management, and Virtual Memory Mechanism.\n The \"Service Learning\" is required in this course. Students are requested to go to communities, junior high schools, elementary schools for their 12-hours \"service learning\".",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 3.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "理解作業系統整體運作原理與內部結構",
      "describe_en": "Understanding global concepts and internal structure for an OS\n"
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "理解作業系統各項資源之管理策略與機制",
      "describe_en": "Understanding the relationship between computer hardware and OS\n"
    }
